+config WEB888_EEPROM_MAC
+	bool "Plant ethaddr from the Web-888 board EEPROM"
+	depends on DM_I2C && I2C_EEPROM
+	help
+	  Web-888 boards keep the per-unit MAC raw at offset 0x10 of the
+	  24c64 EEPROM on i2c0 (chip 0x50). Read it in board_late_init()
+	  (the env store must be ready) and set ethaddr before ethernet
+	  probes, so the GEM and the fdt local-mac-address fixup use the
+	  factory MAC instead of a random one. A pre-existing ethaddr in
+	  the environment wins.
+
 endif
